Add a "Support Aerium" row to the About page.

Asked for directly: a donation link on chrome://settings/help itself, not just
the indirect route through the About page's project link (which already points
at aerium-browser.github.io, via aerium-about-page-project-url.patch).

The new string lives in settings_chromium_strings.grdp, the non-Chrome-branded
variant already used for "Get help with Chromium" - Aerium builds this branch,
not settings_google_chrome_strings.grdp. The existing "report an issue" and
"privacy policy" rows are gated behind _google_chrome/GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING
and compile out entirely for us; the new row and its click handler are placed
outside every such guard so they actually exist in the build, unlike those two.

Opens the site's own #support anchor, which already carries both addresses and
their QR codes, rather than duplicating that content into the browser binary.

Three of these four hunks carry aerium-update-checker.patch's own added
lines as context, because that patch is earlier in the series and inserts
right where this one otherwise would: the strings-provider hunk anchors past
its three new map entries, and the about_page.ts method hunk anchors past its
new onAeriumUpdateClick_() rather than past onHelpClick_() directly.

The about_page.html.ts hunk originally anchored on the "help" cr-link-row
(@click onHelpClick_, $i18n{aboutGetHelpUsingChrome}) - which does not exist
at this tag at all. ungoogled-chromium's own
patches/extra/ungoogled-chromium/remove-uneeded-ui.patch deletes that row
outright, before any aerium-fatih patch runs. `patch`'s fuzzy matching still
found a place to apply the original hunk - fuzz tolerates exactly this kind
of missing context - but the place it found was wrong: it spliced the new
row into the middle of the neighbouring aeriumUpdateCheck
settings-toggle-button's attribute list, between pref-key and label. That
went undetected because nothing between authoring the patch and this fix
ever actually got the build far enough to apply it against the real tree;
every build in between failed earlier, on the unrelated
aerium-first-run-page.patch hunk-count bug. Re-anchored on the
aeriumUpdateAvailable block's own closing `` ` : ''} `` line plus the
following `<if expr="_google_chrome">`, both of which remain after
remove-uneeded-ui.patch and are unique in the file.

Regenerated by applying remove-uneeded-ui.patch's relevant hunks and
aerium-update-checker.patch for real against the pristine 152.0.7977.82
tag, editing that result by hand, and diffing - not against pristine, and
not written blind. Verified end to end: pristine -> remove-uneeded-ui ->
aerium-update-checker -> this patch -> aerium-about-page-share-link.patch
applies with zero fuzz and zero rejected hunks.

